ve matching tags from both the title and content. The replacement strategy with `$0` captures the leading character before the tag and removes just the tag itself, preserving spacing and punctuation correctly. Now I need to verify this handles the regex special characters properly—`Pattern.quote()` will escape any regex metacharacters in the tag text, which is important for safety. Let me trace through the test case to confirm the logic works as expected. I need to make `Pattern` importable. Looking at the existing imports in the file, I see `java.util.regex.Matcher` is already there, so I just need to add `java.util.regex.Pattern` to the imports. I'll update the `removeTag` method to use the pattern with word boundaries instead of the simple string replacement.\n","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}}
