{"type":"assistant","uuid":"fd11bf1c-ce38-4c66-8cc9-a6c9e5827f60","session_id":"4c9c182f-67db-4b23-8a72-daae5ebafea6","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"fd11bf1c-ce38-4c66-8cc9-a6c9e5827f60","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe fix is in place and the build passes. Here's a summary of the fix:\n\n## Bug Analysis\n\n**Root Cause**: In `TagsHelper.removeTag()`, the method used `replaceAll(tagToRemove.getText(), \"\")` which replaces **all** occurrences of the tag text as a substring, not just the specific tag token.\n\n**Example**: If a note contains `#test #testa #testb` and the user unchecks `#test`, the buggy code replaced every occurrence of the substring `\"#test\"` — which matched inside `#testa` and `#testb`, incorrectly stripping them to just `#`.\n\n## Fix\n\nChanged the `removeTag` method in `TagsHelper.java` to use a word-boundary-aware regex pattern:\n\n**Before (buggy):**\n```java\ntitle = title.replaceAll(tagToRemove.getText(), \"\");\ncontent = content.replaceAll(tagToRemove.getText(), \"\");\n```\n\n**After (fixed):**\n```java\nString escapedText = Pattern.quote(tagToRemove.getText());\nString tagPattern = \"(?<!\\\\S)\" + escapedText + \"\\\\b\";\ntitle = title.replaceAll(tagPattern, \"\");\ncontent = content.replaceAll(tagPattern, \"\");\n```\n\nThe fix uses:\n1. **`Pattern.quote()`** — escapes any regex special characters in the tag text (e.g., `#`, `.`, etc.)\n2. **`(?<!\\S)`** — negative lookbehind ensuring the tag is preceded by whitespace or is at the start of the string (i.e., it's a standalone whitespace-delimited token)\n3. **`\\b`** — word boundary at the end, ensuring we don't match partial tags like `#testa` when looking for `#test`"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45649,"output_tokens":401,"cache_read_input_tokens":44032,"total_tokens":46050}}}
